## 2. Plan Header Sections Above `## AC coverage` (`IP10`, `IP11`)

`implementation-plan.md` places two mandatory sections immediately above `## AC coverage` while preserving all standard template sections:

1. **`## Global constraints` (`IP10`)**:
   - Copy verbatim every item-wide value pinned by the approved `requirements.md` / `design.md`, citing its source ID (`BR-NN`, `D-NN`, design section).
   - Every task inherits these constraints automatically without paraphrasing or restating them.
   - Typical item-wide constraints in **{{project_name}}**: {{global_constraint_kinds}}
   - Any value required by tasks but omitted by the spec becomes an open `Q-NN` before Gate 3, never an invented default.
2. **`## Review focus` (`IP11`)**:
   - List up to 5 input classes or failure modes implied by the spec that no standard happy-path check covers (e.g., empty/oversized payload, duplicate submit, concurrent edit, lost connection, permission denial), ordered most-likely first.
   - Each row records: **Input / Failure Mode**, **Expected Behavior** (citing `BR-NN`, `AC-NN`, or `D-NN`), and **Owning Task ID** (`PHASE-NN` task that adds the automated test).
   - Write `None found after checking every AC and BR` only after verifying every `AC-NN` and `BR-NN`.
   - Common review-focus gaps in **{{project_name}}**: {{review_focus_examples}}

