## 4. Branch, Sub-Ticket / Accepted-Phase Commit Checkpoints & Hotfix Tasks (`IP7`, `G2`, `G3`, `M3`, `M10`)

Align every implementation plan with `git-workflow` (`G2`, `G3`, `M3`, `M10`) and the `git-preflight` `D-NN` record:

| Rule | Mandatory Planning Contract |
|---|---|
| **Parent-Ticket Work Branch (`G2`, `M3`)** | Cut one work branch per parent/umbrella ticket from the confirmed base ref: `<type>/<PARENT-TICKET>-<short-description>` (or `<type>/<short-description>` only when no tracker ticket exists). |
| **Verified Commit Checkpoints (`G3`, `M10`)** | Each accepted phase or sub-ticket boundary in the plan maps to an explicit commit checkpoint after its verification gates report `PASS` — never arbitrary mid-phase WIP commits:<br>• **Parent Ticket + Sub-Ticket**: `<type>(<SUB-TICKET>): <summary> [parent: <PARENT-TICKET>, PHASE-NN]`<br>• **Parent Ticket + Multi-Phase (no sub-ticket ID)**: `<type>(<PARENT-TICKET>): [PHASE-NN] <summary>`<br>• **No Ticket ID (user-supplied requirement)**: `<type>(phase-NN): <summary>` |
| **Hotfix Propagation & Human-Only Release Gates (`G5`, `M6`)** | Production hotfix plans include explicit propagation tasks for `{{hotfix_lines}}`. Merging into production (`main`), creating release tags, and triggering production deployments are listed strictly as commands for the user to run (`M6`), never agent tasks. |

